{"name":"Graham Cracker","hex":"#c0a480","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"graham cracker","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A specific cracker made of graham flour, developed in the nineteenth century.","A sweet rectangular cracker, usually made of graham flour and sweetened with honey (and often spiced with cinnamon) and perforated down the middle."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/graham_cracker"}],"entries":[{"title":"Graham cracker","blocks":[{"text":"A graham cracker is a sweet cracker made with graham flour that originated in the United States in the mid-19th century, with commercial development from about 1880, and mass production beginning in 1898 by The National Biscuit Company. It is eaten as a snack food, usually honey- or cinnamon-flavored, and is used as an ingredient in some foods, e.g., in the graham cracker crust for cheesecakes and pies."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Graham-Cracker-Stack.jpg/330px-Graham-Cracker-Stack.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graham_cracker","wikidata":"Q5593383"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/National_Biscuit_Company_graham_crackers%2C_1915.jpg/250px-National_Biscuit_Company_graham_crackers%2C_1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/National_Biscuit_Company_graham_crackers%2C_1915.jpg/500px-National_Biscuit_Company_graham_crackers%2C_1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/National_Biscuit_Company_graham_crackers%2C_1915.jpg/250px-National_Biscuit_Company_graham_crackers%2C_1915.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ANa